      "message": "\u003e \u003e \u003e I should have patched these internally before submitting. I\u0027m just preparing these to be safe. Jonathan, I\u0027ll try to extract some test cases tomorrow.\n\u003e \u003e \n\u003e \u003e ```\n\u003e \u003e cwebp ../libwebp-test-data/bryce.webp -o - |md5sum\n\u003e \u003e ```\n\u003e \u003e \n\u003e \u003e is enough to show the difference between x86/C and Arm.\n\u003e \u003e \n\u003e \u003e x86: eadf89805059c33a93e7f13366b9f68b\n\u003e \u003e Arm: 8a1737f570de92030371eccaadd39f77\n\u003e \n\u003e Another way to do this with the same Arm binary is to use `-noasm` with a build configured with `-DWEBP_DSP_OMIT_C_CODE\u003d0`.\n\n`libwebp-test-data/test_cwebp.sh --exec\u003dcwebp libwebp-test-data/*.webp` would catch this too. bryce is a bit slow, but it might be worth adding that to our presubmit. libwebp-test-data/lossless_color_transform.ppm fails as well.",
